    <dashboard name='Screentime&apos;s Effect on Mental Wellness' type='storyboard'>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-description'>
          <format attr='font-style' id='story-description_10' value='normal' />
          <format attr='font-weight' id='story-description_10' value='normal' />
          <format attr='text-decoration' id='story-description_10' value='none' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='262' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='964' maxwidth='1016' minheight='964' minwidth='1016' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98340' id='7' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98426' x='787' y='830'>
            <zone h='5187' id='8' type-v2='title' w='98426' x='787' y='830'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='93153' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98426' x='787' y='6017'>
              <zone h='10477' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98426' x='787' y='6017' />
              <zone h='82676' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98426' x='787' y='16494'>
                <flipboard active-id='8' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                  <story-points>
                    <story-point caption='INTRODUCTION | Thank you for visiting my LaunchCode Data Analytics final project. Let&apos;s jump in.' captured-sheet='Title Page' id='4' />
                    <story-point caption='BACKGROUND | Information on the project and introducing questions to explore.' captured-sheet='Question' id='9'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <dashboard name='Question'>
                          <zone id='5'>
                            <formatted-text>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='15'>For this project, data was cleaned and analyzed in Python using pandas, numpy, matplotlib, and seaborn before working in Tableau. The link is available in this presentation to view my complete work on GitHub and the dataset on Kaggle.</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='15'>Some questions we might have from looking at the data:</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontsize='8'>Æ </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='15'>- What is screentime&apos;s effect on mental wellness? </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='15'>- Who logs the most screentime?</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='15'>- Does screentime effect groups of people differently? </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Arial' fontsize='15'>- How can we best improve mental wellness? </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                            </formatted-text>
                          </zone>
                        </dashboard>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='BACKGROUND | There were 400 participants in this study on screentime&apos;s effect on mental wellness. Here is a brief background on who they represent.' captured-sheet='Demographics' id='1' />
                    <story-point caption='EXPLORATION | Here we can see correlations between different lifestyle choices and participants&apos; wellness.' captured-sheet='Analysis' id='2'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <worksheet name='8 graph spread'>
                          <selection-collection />
                        </worksheet>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='EXPLORATION | Similarly, we can see how sleep hours, sleep quality, and productivity level all have negative correlations with screentime.' captured-sheet='Exploration' id='3'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <worksheet name='Sleep Quality/Hours/Prod/Wellness/Screen'>
                          <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.1nu5qy615dm9co1ddny8301bqi4e].[none:occupation:nk]'>
                            <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[none:occupation:nk]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                          </filter>
                        </worksheet>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='EXPLORATION | Another consideration is work. Note the higher average daily screentime for students and remote participants.' captured-sheet='Occupation' id='5'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <worksheet name='age/gender/screentime'>
                          <selection-collection>
                            <node-selection select-tuples='false'>
                              <oriented-node-reference orientation='vertical'>
                                <node-reference>
                                  <axis>[federated.1nu5qy615dm9co1ddny8301bqi4e].[avg:screen_time_hours:qk]</axis>
                                </node-reference>
                                <page-reference />
                              </oriented-node-reference>
                            </node-selection>
                          </selection-collection>
                        </worksheet>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='CONCLUSION | Let&apos;s put together some of what we&apos;ve seen.' captured-sheet='Conclusion' id='8'>
                      <currentDeltas>
                        <dashboard name='Conclusion'>
                          <zone id='5'>
                            <formatted-text>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>What have we learned here?</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Æ </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Screentime has the strongest relationship to mental wellness in this study. While increasing the time one spends socializing, exercising, or getting good rest could significantly improve mental wellness and lower stress levels, the option that has the largest impact on mental wellness is limiting screentime. </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>People who work remotely tend to have higher screentime on average, though students and employed people have higher average screentime overall. You may consider looking for a hybrid or in-person job if your goal is lowering your screentime.</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Screentime habits and mental wellness ratings vary greatly across different groups in this study. It would be interesting to dig into that a little more as a continuing business question.</run>
                            </formatted-text>
                          </zone>
                        </dashboard>
                      </currentDeltas>
                      <capturedDeltas>
                        <dashboard name='Conclusion'>
                          <zone id='5'>
                            <formatted-text>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>What have we learned here?</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Æ </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Screentime has the strongest relationship to mental wellness in this study. While increasing the time one spends socializing, exercising, or getting good rest could significantly improve mental wellness and lower stress levels, the option that has the largest impact on mental wellness is limiting screentime. </run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>People who work remotely tend to have higher screentime on average, though students and employed people have higher average screentime overall. You may consider looking for a hybrid or in-person job if your</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>goal is lowering your screentime.</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>Screentime habits and mental wellness ratings vary greatly in this study. It would be</run>
                              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='14'>interesting to dig into that a little more as a continuing business question.</run>
                            </formatted-text>
                          </zone>
                        </dashboard>
                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                  </story-points>
